 ### Hardware Acceleration via Vertex Programs
-A proposed optimization to move feature enhancements onto the graphics card using programmable vertex shaders, avoiding expensive vertex downloads [S4]. Preprocessed points are stored as display lists or vertex arrays in the graphics card’s memory. Vertex programs evaluate the thresholds of feature enhancements; if a vertex falls below the threshold, its coordinates are modified to a position off screen to effectively cull it [S4]. This culling is possible because the system uses vertices rather than polygons, allowing simple thresholding formulae to be implemented directly. However, this technique is not generally possible for polygons due to the lack of connectivity information in vertex programs [S4].
