 ### Flow Illustration via Stippling
-An application of volume stippling to flow data, where flow features (critical points, vortices, etc.) are conveyed with simple strokes, avoiding high-gradient boundary emphasis [S3, unofficial]. Flow data often lacks high gradients, so boundaries are not the main concern. Instead, the method identifies flow features such as vortices, sources, and sinks from the vector field data. Stipples are generated to represent these structures, potentially using silhouette curves and contouring transfer functions to show major structures, avoiding visual clutter [S3, unofficial].
